  "period_note": "Solo (standalone, not consolidated) basis throughout, per project standing rule. MAJOR ASSET-QUALITY DETERIORATION (consistent with the sector-wide FY2024 recognition event): classified investments jump from 13,797m (FY2023) to 59,686m (FY2024), a 4.3x increase; NPL ratio self-computed as classified/gross-loans = 59,686.2/199,192.71 = 29.96% (bank's own reported figure, 29.31%, is close but not exact - both are used and cited). General Provision for Unclassified/Off-Balance-Sheet Investments is nil for the fourth consecutive year; a 49.6m provision for diminution in value of investments appears for the first time. DUAL CRAR DISCLOSURE: the Directors' Report / MD&A narrative states CRAR 'stood at 15.65% on solo basis and 15.26% on consolidated basis' explicitly BECAUSE 'Bangladesh Bank allowed us deferral... for finalizing the audited accounts without adjusting shortfall provisions where classified investments and its corresponding claims... has not been considered'; the same report's formal Pillar-3 'Capital Adequacy' qualitative disclosure instead states CRAR '14.12% on solo basis and 13.79% on consolidated basis' with 'CCB of 4.12% on solo basis' (self-consistent: 14.12%-10.00% minimum=4.12%). The lower, shortfall-inclusive 14.12% (Solo) is used as car_pct here, consistent with this dataset's general preference for recognition over deferral (see NBL/ISLAMIBANK precedent in _HANDOFF.md); 15.65% is recorded as the bank's own alternate, deferral-benefiting headline figure. Deferred tax for FY2024 is not separately legible in the extracted P&L (only the Total Provision for Taxation and Current Tax lines survived OCR); it is calculated here as their residual (Total Tax 1,165,516,909 - Current Tax 1,173,852,730 = -8,335,821), and the resulting PBT-tax=PAT identity reproduces exactly (1,978,100,176 - 1,165,516,909 = 812,583,267), confirming this residual is internally consistent even though its own P&L line was not directly legible. This is the last year of the 'Standard Bank PLC.' name before the bank's Feb-10-2026 rename to 'Standard Islami Bank PLC.'.",
